    "w": 0.52254,
    "h": 0.04941
   },
   "text": "Amplitude Decay of a Spring-Damper System with Symbolic Coefficients"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i1",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.45975,
    "y": 0.22284,
    "w": 0.0805,
    "h": 0.01509
   },
   "text": "D. Spring"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i2",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.44393,
    "y": 0.25372,
    "w": 0.11215,
    "h": 0.01509
   },
   "text": "October 2026"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i3",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.46419,
    "y": 0.3066,
    "w": 0.07163,
    "h": 0.01258
   },
   "text": "Abstract"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i4",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.17398,
    "y": 0.3305,
    "w": 0.65205,
    "h": 0.05786
   },
   "text": "We write the free vibration of a unit mass on a spring with stiffness k and damping coefficient c as a two-state system. The oscillation is periodic with slowly decaying amplitude, and increasing the damping coefficient increases the decay rate while leaving the period nearly unchanged."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i5",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.41474,
    "w": 0.16946,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "1 The system"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i6",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.449,
    "w": 0.54933,
    "h": 0.01377
   },
   "text": "In state variables x (displacement) and y (velocity) the dynamics read"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i7",
   "kind": "formula",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.47586,
    "y": 0.47995,
    "w": 0.39473,
    "h": 0.01377
   },
   "latex": "\\dot { x } = y ,"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i8",
   "kind": "formula",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.44457,
    "y": 0.51089,
    "w": 0.42602,
    "h": 0.01377
   },
   "latex": "\\dot { y } = - k x - c y ."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i9",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.55082,
    "w": 0.35587,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "2 Initial state and coefficients"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i10",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.58508,
    "w": 0.74118,
    "h": 0.03088
   },
   "text": "The mass is released from rest at unit displacement, with the recorded initial state x(0) = 1 and y(0) = 0. The nominal coefficients are k = 2 and c = 0.5."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i11",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.64211,
    "w": 0.15696,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "3 Discussion"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i12",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.67637,
    "w": 0.74118,
    "h": 0.04799
   },
   "text": "The amplitude decays by a fixed factor per cycle set by the damping coefficient, while the oscillation period stays close to the undamped value; small perturbations of the coefficients preserve this picture."
  }
 ]
}